{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "קנה", :translit "kaneh", :gloss "buy"} {:he "לא כי קנה", :translit "lo ki kaneh", :gloss "no, for buy"} {:he "אקנה בכסף מלא", :translit "ekneh be-kesef male", :gloss "I will buy with full silver"} {:he "כי קנו", :translit "ki kanu", :gloss "for they bought"} {:he "אקנה מאותך במחיר", :translit "ekneh me-itekha be-mehir", :gloss "I will buy from you at a price"} {:he "שלא היה יכול לקנות מישראל", :translit "she-lo hayah yachol liknot mi-yisrael", :gloss "that he was not able to buy from an Israelite"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["לא כי קנה" "אקנה בכסף מלא" "כי קנו"]}], :frame {:text "The prohibition derived from Leviticus 25:14, \"or buy from the hand of your fellow,\" is understood to mean one should prefer buying from an Israelite rather than from a gentile (Avodah Zarah 21b–22a, in the sugya discussing purchase of land). David purchased the threshing floor from Aravnah the Jebusite because no Israelite owned the site on the Temple Mount (2 Samuel 24:18–24; the identification of the threshing floor as the Temple Mount site is in rabbinic tradition, e.g., Rashi on 2 Samuel 24:18 citing midrashic sources).", :sources ["Leviticus 25:14" "2 Samuel 24:18–24" "Avodah Zarah 21b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "א", :translit "aleph", :gloss "aleph"} {:he "ל תונו איש את אחיו", :translit "lo tonu ish et achiv", :gloss "do not oppress each man his brother"} {:he "וסמיך ליה", :translit "u-smikh lei", :gloss "and adjacent to it"} {:he "במספר לו", :translit "be-mispar lo", :gloss "by number to him"} {:he "דבר שבמדה ושבמשקל אין בו אונאה", :translit "davar she-be-midah u-va-mishkal ein bo on'ah", :gloss "a thing that is by measure or by weight has no oppression"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["לא תונו איש את אחיו" "במספר לו"]} {:kind :other, :note "Adjacent verses share aleph-lamed linkage: 'Lo tonu' and 'Lecha' both open with aleph-lamed."}], :frame {:text "The Talmud derives from the juxtaposition of Leviticus 25:14 and Leviticus 25:15 that items sold by count, measure, or weight are not subject to the prohibition of price fraud (on'ah), since Leviticus 25:15 introduces \"by number\" immediately after the prohibition in Leviticus 25:14 (Bava Metzia 51a–51b).", :sources ["Leviticus 25:14–15" "Bava Metzia 51a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["לא כי קנה" "אקנה בכסף מלא" "כי קנו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "לא כי קנה", :refs ["1 Chronicles 21:24"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "אקנה בכסף מלא", :refs ["1 Chronicles 21:24"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כי קנו", :refs ["2 Samuel 24:24"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["לא תונו איש את אחיו" "במספר לו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "לא תונו איש את אחיו", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "במספר לו", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Adjacent verses share aleph-lamed linkage: 'Lo tonu' and 'Lecha' both open with aleph-lamed.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:25:42.547663614Z", :model "glm-5.2"}